# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRIVATE DICTATION AND MEETING CONTENT — never commit.
# The archive holds verbatim diarized transcripts of real conversations,
# everything this machine has ever dictated, and the screen context captured
# alongside it. It must never reach a remote, public or private.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
archive/
*.archive/
/notes/
/export/
/exports/
/out/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local copies of Wispr Flow's own store — never commit.
# A snapshot of flow.sqlite is the entire corpus in one file: meetings with AI
# summaries, scratchpad notes, the custom dictionary (which is mostly names,
# employers and project codenames), calendar attendees, and the History and
# FlowLensHistory tables' audio, screenshot, axText and axHTML columns.
# The -wal and -shm sidecars hold uncommitted pages of exactly the same data,
# so they are no less sensitive than the main database. backups/ is the app's
# own rolling copy and is a full second corpus.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
flow.sqlite*
backup-*.sqlite
/backups/
/snapshots/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Wispr Flow application state — never commit.
# session.json is a PLAINTEXT Supabase session: a bearer access_token, a
# refresh token, and the account's email, id and full name. There is no
# keychain entry guarding it; it is a bare file, mode 0666. config.json
# carries the account's name, email, device ids, saved writing samples and
# polish prompts. The logs carry accessibility-tree captures of whatever was
# on screen. These are only ever copied here while debugging, and must never
# be committed even then.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
session.json
config.json
config.json.tmp-*
feature-flags.json
Local State
Preferences
/sentry/
*.log
*.log.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transcript and audio artifacts — never commit.
# refined.ndjson, live.ndjson and speakers.observations.ndjson are verbatim
# diarized transcripts. upload.ogg is raw meeting audio: every voice in the
# room, unredactable, ~16 MB apiece. No test ever needs a real one — fixtures
# are Python literals in conftest.py, never data files, so this blanket
# ignore has no legitimate exception.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.ndjson
*.jsonl
*.ogg
*.opus
*.wav
*.m4a
*.mp3
*.flac
*.webm

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Screen captures — never commit.
# History.screenshot and FlowLensHistory.screenshot are image BLOBs taken at
# dictation time, and NoteImages.data is an image BLOB too. Anything extracted
# from them lands here first. There is no negation for docs/ on purpose: a
# negated ignore pattern is precisely how real data gets committed, and a
# documentation image is rare enough to deserve a deliberate `git add -f` and
# a look at the file before it goes in.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.heic
*.webp
*.gif
*.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — never commit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.enc
credentials.json
secrets.json
*token*.json
*.jwt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Note: uv.lock IS committed on purpose — it pins the dependency graph.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
